<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">N. F. S. Grundtvig</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1783">1783</a>–<a href="/years/1872">1872</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Nikolaj Frederik Severin Grundtvig</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">N. F. S. Grundtvig was a Danish pastor, poet, historian and educator. He wrote some 1,500 hymns and promoted a joyful, popular <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> and Danish national culture. His ideas inspired the folk high schools, adult education colleges for young rural people founded from 1844, which, together with the cooperative movement, transformed the Danish countryside.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/n-f-s-grundtvig.jpg" alt="N. F. S. Grundtvig" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Christian Albrecht Jensen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:N-f-s-grundtvig-portr%C3%A6t.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Cooperative dairies and the folk high schools inspired by N.F.S. <b>Grundtvig</b> later transformed rural life, and the twentieth century built a tax-funded welfare state.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-denmark">Kingdom of Denmark · Socioeconomy</a></li></ul></section>
